      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__bram_1gab305438b0844ddb20139878c21ef0e6b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XBram_CfgInitialize</definition>
        <argsstring>(XBram *InstancePtr, XBram_Config *Config, UINTPTR EffectiveAddr)</argsstring>
        <name>XBram_CfgInitialize</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_bram" kindref="compound">XBram</ref> *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_bram___config" kindref="compound">XBram_Config</ref> *</type>
          <declname>Config</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>UINTPTR</type>
          <declname>EffectiveAddr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Initializes a specific <ref refid="struct_x_bram" kindref="compound">XBram</ref> instance. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Uses a configuration structure provided by the caller. Nothing is done except to initialize InstancePtr.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to an <ref refid="struct_x_bram" kindref="compound">XBram</ref> instance. The memory the pointer references must be pre-allocated by the caller. Further calls to manipulate the driver through the <ref refid="struct_x_bram" kindref="compound">XBram</ref> API must be made with this pointer. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Reference to a structure containing information about a specific BRAM device. This function initializes an InstancePtr object for a specific device specified by Config. This function can initialize multiple instance objects with multiple calls giving different Config information on each call. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">EffectiveAddr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Device base address in the virtual memory address space. The caller is responsible for keeping the address mapping from EffectiveAddr to the device physical base address unchanged once this function is invoked. Unexpected errors may occur if the address mapping changes after this function is called. If address translation is not used, use Config-&gt;BaseAddress for this parameter, passing the physical address instead.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if initialization was successful. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
